# operator_union.skill — CDLC Context Package
# KQLBridge v0.1 | Generate → Test → Distribute → Observe
# ============================================================

## What union does in KQL
Combines rows from multiple tables. Always UNION ALL in v0.1 (no dedup by default in KQL).

## Translation table
| KQL                          | Spark SQL                                              |
|------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------|
| T1 \| union T2              | SELECT * FROM T1 UNION ALL SELECT * FROM T2            |
| T1 \| union T2, T3          | SELECT * FROM T1 UNION ALL SELECT * FROM T2 UNION ALL SELECT * FROM T3 |

## Full examples
```kql
AppLogs | union ErrorLogs, DebugLogs
```
```sql
SELECT * FROM AppLogs
UNION ALL
SELECT * FROM ErrorLogs
UNION ALL
SELECT * FROM DebugLogs
```

## Edge cases
- `union T2, T3` as pipe: the left table (T1) is the implicit first table
- Standalone `union T1, T2` (without preceding pipe): NOT supported in v0.1 grammar
- Subquery union `union (T2 | where ...)`: grammar allows, but complex union subqueries are simplified

## Known limits
- `union withsource=col` metadata column → not supported
- Column schema mismatch: SQL will raise at runtime, not translation time
- UNION DISTINCT (KQL `union kind=outer` equivalent) → v0.2

## Routing rules
- union_op as pipe → SUPPORTED → UnionOp → SparkSQLGenerator._union()
- Standalone union → UNSUPPORTED (use pipe form instead)
